<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Republic of New Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a>–<a href="/years/1858">1858</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> was the state formed by present-day Colombia and Panama after the break-up of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia in 1830–1831. Its government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> faced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-supremes">War of the Supremes</a> of 1839–1842, a civil war of regional leaders during which Panama briefly broke away as the Free State of the Isthmus. In 1858 it was reorganised as the Granadine Confederation, forerunner of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/republic-of-new-granada.jpg" alt="Republic of New Granada" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fibonacci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Granada.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
